       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of ibuprofen. Each 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n\n- **Standard adult maximum:** 3,200 mg/day for prescription use, given as up to 800 mg per dose. Most inpatient regimens stay at or below 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Risks at 6,400 mg/day:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, fluid retention, hypertension, and cardiovascular events. These risks rise with dose even when kidney function is normal.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n1. **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose, which is sometimes used for inflammatory conditions.\n2. **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **400 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is more typical for pain.\n3. **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n4. The dose you wrote, which would need your confirmation that it's intentional.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter it right away. If you want a GI protection note, such as giving it with food, I can add that."
